{"content_hash": "08ec49edbfa737b1", "version_id": 734, "article_id": 74, "level_code": "en_b2", "lang": "en", "level": 4, "level_label": "B2 中高级", "title": "CNN star Christiane Amanpour quits after 43 years", "title_zh": "CNN老牌主播阿曼普宣布离职，干了43年", "has_translation": true, "topic": "business", "source": "guardian_business", "source_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2026/oct/19/christiane-amanpour-leaving-cnn", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1642723865493-9e4d57eca47a?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8OXx8Y2hyaXN0aWFuZSUyMGFtYW5wb3VyfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTI2Mjc2MzR8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Eder Pozo Pérez on Unsplash", "author": "Eder Pozo Pérez", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@ederpozo?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/a-narrow-street-lined-with-buildings-and-flags-1FMCSwvV8F0?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(315, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(353, 46%, 48%)", "label": "BUSINESS", "seed": "937b1a603b6f"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-22", "word_count": 258, "reading_minutes": 1.3, "lead": "One of CNN's most famous journalists is leaving the network after more than four decades. Christiane Amanpour said she will end her show in May and leave the company at the end of June.", "lead_zh": "CNN最知名的记者之一在效力四十多年后要离开了。克里斯蒂安·阿曼普表示，她将在5月结束自己的节目，并于6月底离开公司。", "preview": "Amanpour, 68, joined CNN in 1983 as an assistant on the international assignment desk and later became its chief international anchor. In a ", "preview_zh": "现年68岁的阿曼普于1983年加入CNN，最初在国际新闻编辑部做助理，后来成为首席国际主播。她在周一的声明中说，经过数月的思考和几个不眠之夜，她做出了离开公司的决定。她还为PBS主持一档节目，该节目将在今年年底结束。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 722, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/74/en_b2.mp3", "duration": 94.35, "size_bytes": 567072, "engine": "kokoro", "voice": "af_heart", "word_count": 291, "has_timeline": true, "alternates": [{"voice": "af_bella", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/74/en_b2_af_bella.mp3", "duration": 96.35, "size_bytes": 579024, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 291, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/74/en_b2_af_bella.json"}, {"voice": "am_michael", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/74/en_b2_am_michael.mp3", "duration": 101.65, "size_bytes": 610848, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 291, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/74/en_b2_am_michael.json"}, {"voice": "bf_emma", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/74/en_b2_bf_emma.mp3", "duration": 88.45, "size_bytes": 531648, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 291, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/74/en_b2_bf_emma.json"}, {"voice": "bm_george", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/74/en_b2_bm_george.mp3", "duration": 95.975, "size_bytes": 576864, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 291, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/74/en_b2_bm_george.json"}]}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@91b304e/content/data/versions/734.json", "paragraphs": ["Amanpour, 68, joined CNN in 1983 as an assistant on the international assignment desk and later became its chief international anchor. In a statement on Monday, she said she made the decision to separate from the network after many months of thought and a few sleepless nights. She also hosts a show for PBS, which will finish at the end of this year.", "She looked back on a long career that included covering the first Gulf war, the Bosnian war, Rwanda, Afghanistan, Ukraine and Iran. She said the teams and the friendship mattered most, as they worked together to find facts and evidence. She told her CNN colleagues: \"Always be truthful, not neutral.\" Amanpour has also been open about her treatment for ovarian cancer, which she was diagnosed with in 2021.", "Her departure comes at a difficult moment for CNN, which is now part of a larger media group called Skydance, run by David Ellison with support from his father Larry. Some CNN journalists view the new ownership with doubt because of its perceived closeness to the Trump administration. Her exit is not thought to be directly linked to the takeover, but she said she would always support CNN's history of independent journalism.", "CNN's CEO, Mark Thompson, thanked her for 43 extraordinary years of journalism, loyalty and friendship. He said they had been discussing the decision for some months and that he accepted it was the right time for her. Amanpour said she will keep hosting her podcast and looks forward to interesting new projects in the future."], "paragraphs_zh": ["现年68岁的阿曼普于1983年加入CNN，最初在国际新闻编辑部做助理，后来成为首席国际主播。她在周一的声明中说，经过数月的思考和几个不眠之夜，她做出了离开公司的决定。她还为PBS主持一档节目，该节目将在今年年底结束。", "她回顾了漫长的职业生涯，报道过第一次海湾战争、波黑战争、卢旺达、阿富汗、乌克兰和伊朗。她说，最重要的是团队和彼此的情谊，大家共同努力寻找事实和证据。她对CNN的同事说：“永远要真实，而不是中立。”阿曼普也一直公开谈论自己2021年确诊卵巢癌后的治疗情况。", "她的离开正值CNN的艰难时刻。CNN如今隶属于一个更大的媒体集团Skydance，由大卫·埃里森掌管，并得到其父亲拉里·埃里森的支持。一些CNN记者对新的所有权持怀疑态度，认为它与特朗普政府关系密切。外界认为她的离职与这次收购没有直接关系，但她表示会一直支持CNN独立新闻的传统。", "CNN首席执行官马克·汤普森感谢她43年来出色的新闻工作、忠诚和友谊。他说双方已就这一决定讨论了好几个月，他接受这对她来说是合适的时机。阿曼普表示她会继续主持自己的播客，并期待未来有趣的新项目。"], "body": "Amanpour, 68, joined CNN in 1983 as an assistant on the international assignment desk and later became its chief international anchor. In a statement on Monday, she said she made the decision to separate from the network after many months of thought and a few sleepless nights. She also hosts a show for PBS, which will finish at the end of this year.\n\nShe looked back on a long career that included covering the first Gulf war, the Bosnian war, Rwanda, Afghanistan, Ukraine and Iran. She said the teams and the friendship mattered most, as they worked together to find facts and evidence. She told her CNN colleagues: \"Always be truthful, not neutral.\" Amanpour has also been open about her treatment for ovarian cancer, which she was diagnosed with in 2021.\n\nHer departure comes at a difficult moment for CNN, which is now part of a larger media group called Skydance, run by David Ellison with support from his father Larry. Some CNN journalists view the new ownership with doubt because of its perceived closeness to the Trump administration. Her exit is not thought to be directly linked to the takeover, but she said she would always support CNN's history of independent journalism.\n\nCNN's CEO, Mark Thompson, thanked her for 43 extraordinary years of journalism, loyalty and friendship. He said they had been discussing the decision for some months and that he accepted it was the right time for her. Amanpour said she will keep hosting her podcast and looks forward to interesting new projects in the future.", "body_zh": "现年68岁的阿曼普于1983年加入CNN，最初在国际新闻编辑部做助理，后来成为首席国际主播。她在周一的声明中说，经过数月的思考和几个不眠之夜，她做出了离开公司的决定。她还为PBS主持一档节目，该节目将在今年年底结束。\n\n她回顾了漫长的职业生涯，报道过第一次海湾战争、波黑战争、卢旺达、阿富汗、乌克兰和伊朗。她说，最重要的是团队和彼此的情谊，大家共同努力寻找事实和证据。她对CNN的同事说：“永远要真实，而不是中立。”阿曼普也一直公开谈论自己2021年确诊卵巢癌后的治疗情况。\n\n她的离开正值CNN的艰难时刻。CNN如今隶属于一个更大的媒体集团Skydance，由大卫·埃里森掌管，并得到其父亲拉里·埃里森的支持。一些CNN记者对新的所有权持怀疑态度，认为它与特朗普政府关系密切。外界认为她的离职与这次收购没有直接关系，但她表示会一直支持CNN独立新闻的传统。\n\nCNN首席执行官马克·汤普森感谢她43年来出色的新闻工作、忠诚和友谊。他说双方已就这一决定讨论了好几个月，他接受这对她来说是合适的时机。阿曼普表示她会继续主持自己的播客，并期待未来有趣的新项目。", "text": "Amanpour, 68, joined CNN in 1983 as an assistant on the international assignment desk and later became its chief international anchor. In a statement on Monday, she said she made the decision to separate from the network after many months of thought and a few sleepless nights. She also hosts a show for PBS, which will finish at the end of this year. She looked back on a long career that included covering the first Gulf war, the Bosnian war, Rwanda, Afghanistan, Ukraine and Iran. She said the teams and the friendship mattered most, as they worked together to find facts and evidence. She told her CNN colleagues: \"Always be truthful, not neutral.\" Amanpour has also been open about her treatment for ovarian cancer, which she was diagnosed with in 2021. Her departure comes at a difficult moment for CNN, which is now part of a larger media group called Skydance, run by David Ellison with support from his father Larry. Some CNN journalists view the new ownership with doubt because of its perceived closeness to the Trump administration. Her exit is not thought to be directly linked to the takeover, but she said she would always support CNN's history of independent journalism. CNN's CEO, Mark Thompson, thanked her for 43 extraordinary years of journalism, loyalty and friendship. He said they had been discussing the decision for some months and that he accepted it was the right time for her. Amanpour said she will keep hosting her podcast and looks forward to interesting new projects in the future.", "vocab": [{"word": "anchor", "pos": "noun", "zh": "主播，新闻节目主持人", "note": "chief international anchor 首席国际主播", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "decorated", "pos": "adj", "zh": "获得多项荣誉的", "note": "常指获奖很多的人", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "venerated", "pos": "adj", "zh": "受人尊敬的", "note": "比 respected 更正式", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "fledging", "pos": "adj", "zh": "刚起步的，初建的", "note": "文中为 fledgling 的变体", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "separate from", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "从……脱离，离开", "note": "此处指离开公司", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "camaraderie", "pos": "noun", "zh": "同志情谊，团队友情", "note": "指同事间的亲密关系", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "battle to", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "奋力去做，努力争取", "note": "battle to seek the facts 努力寻找事实", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "without fear nor favor", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "不偏不倚，无所畏惧", "note": "新闻界常用表达", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "open about", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "坦率谈论，不隐瞒", "note": "be open about sth", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "conglomerate", "pos": "noun", "zh": "企业集团", "note": "media conglomerate 媒体集团", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "perceived", "pos": "adj", "zh": "被认为的，外界眼中的", "note": "perceived closeness 被认为关系密切", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "root for", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "支持，为……加油", "note": "rooting for CNN 支持CNN", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "fetched_at": "2026-10-22T00:07:12.314662", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Amanpour", "s": 0.3, "e": 0.925, "sm": 300, "em": 925, "cs": 0, "ce": 8, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": ",", "s": 0.925, "e": 1.012, "sm": 925, "em": 1012, "cs": 8, "ce": 9, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "68", "s": 1.012, "e": 1.85, "sm": 1012, "em": 1850, "cs": 10, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": ",", "s": 1.85, "e": 1.962, "sm": 1850, "em": 1962, "cs": 12, "ce": 13, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "joined", "s": 1.962, "e": 2.362, "sm": 1962, "em": 2362, "cs": 14, "ce": 20, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "CNN", "s": 2.362, "e": 2.925, "sm": 2362, "em": 2925, "cs": 21, "ce": 24, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "in", "s": 2.925, "e": 3.05, "sm": 2925, "em": 3050, "cs": 25, "ce": 27, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "1983", "s": 3.05, "e": 4.338, "sm": 3050, "em": 4337, "cs": 28, "ce": 32, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "as", "s": 4.338, "e": 4.487, "sm": 4337, "em": 4487, "cs": 33, "ce": 35, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "an", "s": 4.487, "e": 4.575, "sm": 4487, "em": 4575, "cs": 36, "ce": 38, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "assistant", "s": 4.575, "e": 5.15, "sm": 4575, "em": 5150, "cs": 39, "ce": 48, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": "on", "s": 5.15, "e": 5.262, "sm": 5150, "em": 5262, "cs": 49, "ce": 51, "si": 0}, {"i": 12, "w": "the", "s": 5.263, "e": 5.375, "sm": 5262, "em": 5374, "cs": 52, "ce": 55, "si": 0}, {"i": 13, "w": "international", "s": 5.375, "e": 6.05, "sm": 5375, "em": 6049, "cs": 56, "ce": 69, "si": 0}, {"i": 14, "w": "assignment", "s": 6.05, "e": 6.525, "sm": 6050, "em": 6524, "cs": 70, "ce": 80, "si": 0}, {"i": 15, "w